From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Turcios <turcioskevinr@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 03:49:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Scons: Support C level PGO with clang, and in standalone and
 onefile modes

With clang, "--pgo-c" waited for a gcc profile file that never appears.
Now the instrumented binary writes LLVM raw profiles, one per process,
which are merged with the "llvm-profdata" of the compiler's LLVM, and
the final build compiles with the merged profile.

In standalone and onefile modes, the instrumented binary ran before the
distribution existed, so it could not find its DLLs and data files.
Now it is trained in a complete distribution, which is then created
again for the final binary.

For zig, which ships no profile runtime, PGO now reports that clearly
instead of failing to link.

Co-authored-by: wtfyd-agent[bot] <328989958+wtfyd-agent[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Signed-off-by: Kevin Turcios <turcioskevinr@gmail.com>
